-- The REFUSAL exhibit for the DMN exporter (ruling D1, accepted 2026-09-05;
-- `specs/todo/IMPLICIT-PROPS-DESIGN.md` §11.9.1).
--
-- `REFUSE "…"` is L4's way of saying "the model does not cover this" — a
-- determinate outcome that is neither a value nor an error, uncatchable by any
-- rule, observable only at the boundary. DMN has no such outcome. Its whole
-- vocabulary for "no answer" is FEEL's single `null`, which also spells "there
-- is none" and "the engine could not compute it".
--
-- This module is the regression pin for what the exporter does about that.
-- Before D1 it wrote the L4 source text `REFUSE "…"` into a `<literalExpression>`,
-- and KIE 8.44.0.Final then failed to compile the WHOLE FILE
-- (`ERROR [ERR_COMPILING_FEEL] … syntax error`, `VERDICT … <<< FAILED`), which is
-- why no legal-corpus refusal could migrate off `ASSUME`. Now a refusal is FEEL
-- `null`, the author's reason is carried in the artifact, and the fidelity
-- report says at what cost.
--
-- ONE OF EACH POSITION A REFUSAL CAN OCCUPY, because they are different code
-- paths and each one is measured separately by `refuse.cases.json`:
--
--   * `no fee is prescribed before commencement on 1983-01-01`
--        a nullary decision whose WHOLE BODY is a refusal. It has no rows, so
--        it becomes a boxed `<literalExpression>` whose text is `null`, and the
--        reason has nowhere to go but the `<decision>`'s own `<description>`.
--        This is the Reg CF shape (house style: one named definition per
--        refusal, PROPS-REDTEAM §2.8);
--   * `the filing fee`
--        a dated law-time chain (§15) whose FLOOR ARM is that refusal. The
--        floor row is KEPT and answers `null`; D1 measured that omitting it is
--        engine-identical, and keeping it is the arm that keeps the reason
--        where a reader of the table is already looking;
--   * `the fee with surcharge`
--        a plain arithmetic decision downstream of a refusal, so the exhibit
--        shows what a real engine does with `null * 2` rather than asserting it;
--   * `the discount`
--        an INLINE refusal in an `OTHERWISE` arm — no named definition — so the
--        reason lands on that `<rule>`'s `<description>`;
--   * `the band`
--        an ENUM-valued refusal, which is the one shape where the two target
--        engines disagreed. See the block below.
--
-- THE ENUM CASE, AND WHY IT IS HERE. An enum-valued decision emits
-- `<outputValues>` naming its constructors (§3.1/§3.2), and a refusing row then
-- answers a value that list does not contain. MEASURED 2026-09-05, before the
-- repair: KIE 8.44.0.Final enforces `<outputValues>` at RUN TIME and FAILS the
-- decision — "Invalid result value on rule #3, output #1. Value null does not
-- match list of allowed values" — while Camunda 8.7.6 (zeebe-dmn) does not
-- check it at all and returns the null silently, 0 errors. One artifact, two
-- meanings. The exporter now widens THAT TABLE's `<outputValues>` by the FEEL
-- keyword `null` (and reports `D-OUTPUTVALUES-NULL`, Lossy); the enum's own
-- `<itemDefinition>`/`<allowedValues>` is untouched, because a separate probe
-- measured that widening the type does NOT stop the KIE error and widening the
-- table does. The pre-repair KIE error is pinned as a negative control in
-- `not-ok/refuse-enum-unwidened.dmn`, so the divergence cannot quietly return.
--
-- THE dmnmd PROJECTION OF THIS MODULE CARRIES NO TABLES, and that is the
-- finding rather than a defect in the fixture: dmnmd's cell grammar — a number,
-- an integer range, or a bare token — has no `null` and no date, so every table
-- here is omitted. A bare `null` cell would be read back by dmnmd as the STRING
-- "null", which is the one outcome worse than omitting the table.
--
-- What `refuse.dmn.md` DOES carry is one `<!-- OMITTED: … -->` marker per
-- dropped decision, naming it and saying why. That was added 2026-09-05 after
-- measuring what a user actually gets: `l4 export --to dmn-md` exits 0, prints
-- a one-line tally on stderr, and used to write a file containing a heading and
-- nothing else — so the committed artifact, the thing a reader opens and a
-- reviewer diffs, said nothing whatever about the tables it was missing.
-- `refuse.md.fidelity.txt` still carries the located list with codes.
--
-- WHAT THIS EXHIBIT DOES NOT SHOW. It does not migrate any legal-corpus site:
-- `regcf.l4`, `dmn/gst-rate.l4` and `dmn/ymd-dates.l4` still spell their
-- pre-commencement floor as an `ASSUME` the engine harness supplies as `-1`.
-- That migration is a separate change, and this file is what makes it safe to
-- attempt.
--
-- The heading below is load-bearing: `l4 export --to=dmn` with no
-- `--model-name` takes the model name from the outermost `§`.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

§ `Refusal`
    GIVEN `the claim amount` IS A NUMBER

-- Required by the rule-version axis: an unpinned `RULES EFFECTIVE DATE` read
-- resolves to the localized current day, and localization needs a timezone.
TIMEZONE IS "Asia/Singapore"

GIVETH A DATE
`commencement` MEANS YMD 1983 1 1

GIVETH A DATE
`the transition day` MEANS YMD 2026 1 1

-- Position 1: the whole body is a refusal. House style is one NAMED definition
-- per refusal, carrying its own `@ref`, so that every arm reaching it reads as
-- a citation rather than as a repeated sentence.
@ref ruling R2, CORPUS-TRACK §8 — below commencement there is nothing to answer
GIVETH A NUMBER
`no fee is prescribed before commencement on 1983-01-01` MEANS
    REFUSE "no fee is prescribed before commencement on 1983-01-01"

-- Position 2: a law-time chain whose floor arm is that refusal. This is the
-- shape `gst-rate.l4` and the Reg CF corpus both have, with the `ASSUME` bottom
-- replaced by the construct that was designed for it.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the filing fee` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `RULES EFFECTIVE DATE` AT LEAST `the transition day` THEN 1000
           IF `RULES EFFECTIVE DATE` AT LEAST `commencement`       THEN 250
           OTHERWISE `no fee is prescribed before commencement on 1983-01-01`

-- Position 3: what a refusal does to arithmetic downstream of it. FEEL
-- propagates null through `*`; the cases assert that rather than assuming it.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the fee with surcharge` MEANS `the filing fee` TIMES 2

-- Position 4: an INLINE refusal, with no named definition, so the reason has
-- only the row's own `<description>` to live on.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the discount` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the claim amount` AT LEAST 1000 THEN 100
           IF `the claim amount` AT LEAST 100  THEN 10
           OTHERWISE REFUSE "no discount is prescribed for a claim below 100"

-- Position 5: the enum case. `Band` keeps its exact declared domain on its
-- `<itemDefinition>`; only `the band`'s own `<outputValues>` admits `null`.
DECLARE Band IS ONE OF standard, reduced, exempt

GIVETH A Band
`the band` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the claim amount` AT LEAST 1000 THEN standard
           IF `the claim amount` AT LEAST 100  THEN reduced
           OTHERWISE REFUSE "no band is prescribed for a claim below 100"
